      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, it is intentional to disable the modules with the wrong interface version. For example, for a certain device may have KMI version X in boot.img, then building the APEX named KMI version Y with the given boot.img is just wrong.\n\nSee https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/system/extras/+/1371345/22/gki/build/gki.go#232. Technically, the enabled flag can be set in the last \"_check_kmi_version\" module (L155 in that file), but I think they should be disabled altogether. In any case, I\u0027ll need this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "4343b7ec_d13ee826",
      "revId": "9ffe5cc2335cf1774e3f960d1827df5e07f220ad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
