      "writtenOn": "2020-08-06T01:57:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also see bug b/162888350 on checkbuild on aosp_crosshatch (and any legacy devices that does not install GKI APEXes). On these devices, I need to disable the _bootimage_kernel_release_file module defined here:\n\nhttps://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/system/extras/+/1371345/22/gki/build/gki.go#118\n\n... because their boot image simply can\u0027t be parsed by extract_kernel.py; treehugger catches this:\n\nhttps://android-build.googleplex.com/builds/treetop/android-review/1371345?ref\u003dCOMMENT\u0026revision\u003d17\u0026workplanId\u003dL28600000655279463\n\nRight now, even though the only possible value of BOARD_KERNEL_MODULE_INTERFACE_VERSIONS is 5.4-android12-0 (for Android 12), it is unset on devices that does not support GKI APEX. So, I can use it to determine whether the GKI APEX should be built and installed. In Android 13 and beyond, there may be other values for BOARD_KERNEL_MODULE_INTERFACE_VERSIONS, and it should just work by setting the value accordingly. That\u0027s why I am not using a boolean flag for GKI APEX support.",
      "parentUuid": "425ba5d7_c83d4348",
      "revId": "9ffe5cc2335cf1774e3f960d1827df5e07f220ad",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    }
